{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/334844-how-do-you-exalt-a-solar-circle","id":334844,"title":"How do you exalt a Solar Circle?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-08T23:06:17-08:00","id":334844,"title":"How do you exalt a Solar Circle?","content":"Beginning as mortals in a Solar game is fun as you get that rush of power when you exalt, but I have a hard time figuring out how to exalt these characters at the same time. I guess one possibility is to throw them into a challenging situation beyond the limits of mortals, like a fae or beastmen attack and have them all exalt in a glorious fight, but it sometimes feels difficult to justify the social or intellectual characters earning the exaltation in these situations. Another possibility is to have the characters naturally earn their exaltations one or two at a time as appropriate situations arise, but there can be problems when the first person to exalt becomes a sponge for every epic deed, and the mortals get left behind.<br /> <br /> Personally I like the idea that the UCS or even the Exaltations themselves upon seeing a moment where a individual deserves to exalt, might decide to exalt the people around him who have the potential to be great Solars, even if it isn't their exact moment to earn the exaltation through action. So a young backwater priest might stand up to an immaculate monk and exalt Zenith, but this would instigate the retired soldier, scholarly herbalist, local hunter, and visiting merchant to exalt Dawn, Twilight, Night, and Eclipse as well. They now get to contribute to this momentous moment even if they didn't directly act to start it.<br /> <br /> How have you handled this process in your games?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T23:44:43-08:00","id":334874,"title":"","content":"Well something to remember is that while the more epic deeds are more easily accomplished by an exalt they aren't honestly as impressive when done by an exalt. I mean don't get me wrong a I think you need extenuating circumstances to make holding your own in a duel against a rhaksha lord not an impressive feat. Just that not having charms, the soak benefit, or potential boost of skill from a past life would make the same thing more impressive for a mortal. <br /> <br /> To quote Superman, &quot;It's easier to do when you're bulletproof.&quot;<br /> <br /> As for exalting the entire group I'd say a major military battle could do well since it would allow for a variety of situations for a pc to have their own moment of awesome to justify the exaltation. It also helps since different moments make it feel more personal than say the whole lot exalting in the middle of a brawl.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T00:13:13-08:00","id":334904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/334844-how-do-you-exalt-a-solar-circle?p=334874#post334874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for exalting the entire group I'd say a major military battle could do well since it would allow for a variety of situations for a pc to have their own moment of awesome to justify the exaltation. It also helps since different moments make it feel more personal than say the whole lot exalting in the middle of a brawl.</div> </div> </div> </div>A friend actually suggested an extended attack on a town, where you can have people fighting on the front lines, infiltrating the enemies forces, tending to the wounded, rallying the reserves, and seeking aid from a neighboring town, all at the same time.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T00:38:42-08:00","id":334909,"title":"","content":"This is the main thing that always put me off running a mortals-who-become Exalts game, even though I've actually played two mortals who became Exalts in-game and absolutely loved doing so.*<br /> I like the idea of a military battle as giving each person an opportunity to do something Exalt-worthy, because being Exalted because you were standing near someone doing something awesome is going to feel pretty lame to the other players.<br /> If you want to be hardcore (and this only works with some players, so you'll have to decide based on your playgroup), have them in a battle, and try to give them opportunities for heroics. If they avoid the heroics... then they just die like chumps in the battle. Most will try I imagine, but it depends. Then they can make a new Solar character who can join the band next session, since he/she heard that some people had Exalted in this battle.<br /> Another possibility, if you're happy to allow Infernals and Abyssals, is that you give them the opportunity for heroics. If they try to be heroic and don't fluff it, they become Solars (Lunars also works fine of course if that's what they'd prefer). If they try, but botch their first few rolls or something, so it feels ridiculous for them to be Solars, then they die and become Abyssals by a rogue Black Exaltation. If they fail to be heroic... a few days later, while they're moping around with their now Solar buddies, a demon turns up and offers them an Exaltation as well. Of course, since they'll then be hanging around with Solars, I imagine when some other demons turn up from Hell and go &quot;hey, come back with us&quot; then the Solars are likely to stab them in the face and the group can happily continue.<br /> I recognise of course, that this is a pretty radical approach and won't work for a lot of players.<br /> <br /> *The first time was as a mortal in a short-term mortal game. We were a Realm-aligned special operations squad trying to drive the Bull out of Linowan. I exalted after hopping from canoe to canoe across a river during a battle and clubbing a water-aspected Icewalker Dragonblood in a warstrider, in the face (well, warstrider helmet). I didn't quite knock him out, but I came close (I did 6 bashing to him, so close!). So when I exalted as a Lunar, it felt awesome, even though I then had to flee before my own side killed me. But that was one guy, the rest of the party carried on as mortals, because you're not going to get that kind of thing happening for 5 people all in the same scene.<br /> The second time, I was playing a mortal in a Celestial game. Anyway, we were trying to rescue my character's girlfriend from an evil Twilight and his psychotic AI buddy. We got into the underground manse, found the chamber where he was keeping her chained up, fought him, and defeated him. And then I exalted as a Lunar. Now, obviously I had just gone toe-to-toe with a Solar with MA 5 who was trying to rip my head off with Wood Dragon Claw, to save the Raksha I loved... but actually, I think I did like one bashing damage to him, if that. It was the Celestials with me who actually knocked him out. So, while it was obviously the most fitting moment for my character to Exalt, I didn't actually feel like my character really deserved it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T01:09:17-08:00","id":334917,"title":"","content":"I would think that, to justify exalting an entire circle the group of persons in question would need to have a linked destiny and said destiny would have to be something suitably significant that a single solar could not accomplish it alone. That leaves you with kind of a short list of things (killing deathlords, stopping the reclamation, raising lost Saigoth from the depths of the underworld, BIG things). Not knowing the particulars of the group in question it's hard to say what circumstances would vault them down that path. A joint encounter with a suitably important McGuffin could do the job - ie. everyone touches the Simaril and...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1j0RQNTrhSQVIjBJw3555qA1S9Hih1SRwychiPhEwm9k/pub\" target=\"_blank\">Whitescrub Tundra Project</a>: a fan-made setting reference for Exalted 3e.<br /> <a href=\"https://www.fanfiction.net/s/10769032/1/\" target=\"_blank\">Edge of Underleaves</a> A pair of dragon-blooded dare the jungles of the southwest.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4060-mechalich","name":"Mechalich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4060_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"133"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T02:31:44-08:00","id":334931,"title":"","content":"Eh, Ex3 Exaltation will be more &quot;Chose of the God&quot; than &quot;Do Awesome thing, Got your lottery Exaltation&quot;, so the whole Circle getting Exalted at the same time wouldn't raised my eyebrow one bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T02:43:31-08:00","id":334932,"title":"","content":"Under the Ex2 model, I'd suggest going with the battle and, here's my addition... the intellectuals get theirs *first*, attempting to win an epic duel of wits with the enemy and outplot and outplan and inspire the motley band of soldiers they have to work with... and then it's not enough, because they're not fighty Solars, but then...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T02:56:19-08:00","id":334940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/334844-how-do-you-exalt-a-solar-circle?p=334909#post334909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to be hardcore (and this only works with some players, so you'll have to decide based on your playgroup), have them in a battle, and try to give them opportunities for heroics. If they avoid the heroics... then they just die like chumps in the battle.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <b>ST:</b> \u201cYou managed to survive the battle. Congratulations! You trip on a rock and fall onto your spear 15 times. Time to roll a new PC.\u201d<br /> <br /> <b>Player:</b> \u201cWhat?!\u201d<br /> <br /> <b>ST</b>: \u201cYour PC failed to be a hero, so now you are dead. You didn\u2019t rush into the burning temple to save that priest. You didn\u2019t sneak by that patrol to poison the enemy camp. You fled the field when it was obvious that your unit was going to be wiped out. And you failed to seduce the deathknight when he captured the town.\u201d<br /> <br /> <b>Player:</b> \u201cHe was covered in entrails! You said he literally wrapped the general\u2019s intestines around his neck like Mr. T wears gold chains.\u201d<br /> <br /> <b>ST: </b>\u201cIf it were a sexy deathknight obviously looking for a hook-up, seducing them wouldn\u2019t be sufficiently heroic.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 12-09-2014, 06:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T04:48:02-08:00","id":335035,"title":"","content":"Well it's true, it wouldn't be a challenge, would it!<br /> <br /> Actually, I think finding an opportunity for the player whose character concept is world's greatest lover to show their stuff during or before a battle would be kind of amusing. Perhaps they could attempt to seduce the enemy general or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T06:17:32-08:00","id":335094,"title":"","content":"In Shogun 2, Shirabyoshi and Geisha units both have the ability to &quot;distract&quot; an enemy force, and prevent them from moving for a month (or 4 months, depending on your game mode). In the right context, this means their skills at dancing, serving tea, and making conversation are so amazing that a whole army of 2000+ soldiers will think that it's OK to just sit outside in a field in enemy territory in the middle of winter to watch them instead of going and sieging a city like they were supposed to be doing.<br /> <br /> Anyone who can do that without charms deserves to Exalt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 12-09-2014, 09:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T06:28:14-08:00","id":335103,"title":"","content":"Indeed! I imagine, to be fair, that they're distracting just the generals, who keep making excuses not to leave so they can stay at the &quot;tea house&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T08:28:05-08:00","id":335220,"title":"","content":"Why do they all have to Exalt at the same time? I'd draw it out over 2-3 different sessions. All at once feels way too forced/cliche.<br /> <br /> And you could still do this with the one battle. When confronted with an inadequate amount or inferior quality of materials to make barricades and battlements, someone Exalts who can utilize their Craft and possibly Occult to spell the process up. While rallying the demoralized troops, the social person Exalts. When the clash of battle actually happens, the sneaky guy Exalts when he causes mayhem among the enemy and the super-righty guy Exalts when he solos the enemy leader's bodyguards and him despite being badly wounded/outnumbered.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/334844-how-do-you-exalt-a-solar-circle?p=334932#post334932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Under the Ex2 model, I'd suggest going with the battle and, here's my addition... the intellectuals get theirs *first*, attempting to win an epic duel of wits with the enemy and outplot and outplan and inspire the motley band of soldiers they have to work with... and then it's not enough, because they're not fighty Solars, but then...</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI feel like this kinda devalues the think-y people a little. A brilliant but non-warrior Solar putting their mind to it is able to re-enact the invasion of 1066 and win as Harold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 12-09-2014, 11:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T08:45:45-08:00","id":335229,"title":"","content":"Our storyteller had us tie each of our characters to a particular emotion that our character identified with. We didn't exalt together, but we didn't really care to. Starting as a heroic mortal gave us each enough power to play with until we got there. Each of us eventually came to an awesome scene where we embodied our emotion and underwent a cathartic release where exaltation was the only path to survival or success. I think it worked well - certainly encouraged role playing since gaining Essence was tied with character psychology.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4297-explodingjoe","name":"ExplodingJoe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4297_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T09:35:17-08:00","id":335245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/334844-how-do-you-exalt-a-solar-circle?p=335220#post335220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do they all have to Exalt at the same time? I'd draw it out over 2-3 different sessions. All at once feels way too forced/cliche.<br /> <br /> And you could still do this with the one battle. When confronted with an inadequate amount or inferior quality of materials to make barricades and battlements, someone Exalts who can utilize their Craft and possibly Occult to spell the process up. While rallying the demoralized troops, the social person Exalts. When the clash of battle actually happens, the sneaky guy Exalts when he causes mayhem among the enemy and the super-righty guy Exalts when he solos the enemy leader's bodyguards and him despite being badly wounded/outnumbered.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200bI feel like this kinda devalues the think-y people a little. A brilliant but non-warrior Solar putting their mind to it is able to re-enact the invasion of 1066 and win as Harold.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure... but this Creation, which is a profoundly unfair place. &quot;I've destroyed your armies with a cunning ambush, Reaper-of-Souls!&quot; &quot;That's nice. I can slaughter yours single-handedly. Still, this was definitely inconvenient.&quot; says the Deathknight...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T13:18:29-08:00","id":335409,"title":"","content":"In the recent game I've been storytelling I've done it by degree's as my players demonstrated awesome creativity during gaming, as follows...<br /> <br /> 1) Our Night Caste, 1st to Exalt (and a generally awesome player by the way) Exalted when he used White Veil Style to Poison a Raksha Noble that I had no intention of forcing the players to actually fight.He drew the creature in, gained its trust, drank a vial of handy poison manufactured by a PC alchemist, internalized the poison through a White Veil Technique (yeah, my Creation is a little different) and then stabbed her in the back.<br /> <br /> 2) Our Eclipse Caste, at the tail end of that same session, Exalted after negotiating safe passage, the release of captives, and then seducing a Heart Chakra Argent Blossom (again, my Creation varies in some respects). How did he do this? Dancing. Dancing, and some very impressive stunts.<br /> <br /> 3) Twilight number 1 Exalted two sessions later when he faced down a caravan of Reavers after trapping them between a large cliff and a bridge over a narrow river. When they refused to surrender he cast Death of Obsidian Butterflies.<br /> <br /> 4) Twilight number 2 (the alchemist) Exalted while the Circle was clearing out a labor camp run by Yozi worshipers. She got caught between escape and leaving prisoners to die at the claws of of a Blood Ape. Since she bought up Past Lives to 5 I have her temporary access to one charm of any essence level &lt;6. The player chose a homebrew E5 larceny charm that allowed her to steal the blood ape's sorcerously bound loyalty, and then direct it against the cultists. <br /> <br /> 5) Our Dawn Caste Ronin Kenshin-alike (and brother to the Night) and last to Exalt did so when facing down a minor river god who blamed him for killing his mortal lover, a local petty lord that was partially responsible for bringing the characters together. While the party was in full-spring <i>running the hell </i><i>away</i> mode, the Dawn-to-be compelled an earlier instance in which he had heard a Demon Harpist <i>Play Time</i> and allowed him to break the river gods essence-induced fear effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T13:44:23-08:00","id":335448,"title":"","content":"I find that is it much more fun to not exalt the players as a group but have little mini-events that explain why each character was chosen. My players usually find it rather amusing to watch each other exaltations play out. One particular character is still famed for his Scooby Do chase scene during an exaltation.<br /> <br /> Don't feel like you need to have everyone exalt at the same time. It is perfectly fine for one character to exalt months or even years before everyone else and just happen upon each other. A solar would most likely be interested if they just happened upon someone in the midst of their own exaltation or hear about another solar who just happens to be in the area. Even better if they have already got themselves embroiled into a local story.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4498-ardis","name":"Ardis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T13:55:48-08:00","id":335454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/334844-how-do-you-exalt-a-solar-circle?p=335245#post335245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure... but this Creation, which is a profoundly unfair place. &quot;I've destroyed your armies with a cunning ambush, Reaper-of-Souls!&quot; &quot;That's nice. I can slaughter yours single-handedly. Still, this was definitely inconvenient.&quot; says the Deathknight...</div> </div> </div> </div>If you were assuming a bunch of mortal fighting an Abyssal-led force, that's a very different scenario than I think is normal, or that I was considering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T20:29:48-08:00","id":356191,"title":"","content":"I'm about to start a Mortals-to-Solars/Lunars War-based campaign myself, and I *intend* to do something a bit odd-ball, and would like feedback.<br /> <br /> Basically, since I KNOW there are going to be staggered Exaltations, and I intend to make it fully to each character's strengths that cause the Exaltations (Warrior on the battlefield, Strategist reacting to an unexpected strategum by the enemy, etc), I'm also aware that this will make for a VERY mixed group very fast. It will probably take two or three sessions, but my basic intent is that, for the scene a person Exalts in, they gain an effective 5 in all of their primary block's Attributes, and all of the Caste Abilities, and if it isn't their Favored, an effective 5 in that as well, and Willpower spikes to 10, with all spent Willpower recovered as if Limit broken. They also gain access to ALL the excellencies for those given Abilities or Attributes if they go Lunar, again, for the length of the scene.At the end of the scene in question, they drop back down to whatever they had before. They still gain permanently Ess 2 and minimum Will of 5, but all the other benefits of Exalting (increased Attributes, Abilities, any Bonus points spent of Ess 3/4, Backgrounds, etc) would need an extended downtime to justify, which will be provided just after the last party member's Exaltation. Said downtime wouldn't be very long, just &quot;long enough&quot; for the characters to get to understand those crazy visions they saw on the battlefield, and learn a little bit about how to apply their sudden new strengths, so maybe a week or two of marching with the army. Then their (former?) bosses approach,and now they are LEADING the army, though not necessarily commanding it. Or running from it, depending on what they do. Mwa ha.Ha ha ha.<br /> <br /> Now that I write it out, perhaps half of the difference in Ability points as an instant boost, and maybe two Charms, both of which must be from Caste or Favored instead of the normal 10 stick around as well? That way they aren't entirely Mortals+, but they aren't full on top-tier-death-machines either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4623-onigato","name":"Onigato","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T21:27:18-08:00","id":356241,"title":"","content":"I assume the idea of not giving them all the charms and so on straight away, is so that the group isn't too imbalanced?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T21:43:06-08:00","id":356264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/334844-how-do-you-exalt-a-solar-circle?p=335454#post335454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you were assuming a bunch of mortal fighting an Abyssal-led force, that's a very different scenario than I think is normal, or that I was considering.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My point was not the specific Abyssal idea, but to use it as an example of a situation where &quot;just&quot; a brilliant tactician - or &quot;just&quot; a brilliant warrior (a lone newly Exalted Dawn caste can still be overwhelmed) - is not going to be sufficient.<br /> <br /> And it's not *normal*, but it's by no means unheard of - there are a LOT of different kinds of powerful beings in Creation who can give a newly fledged Solar a run for their money, particularly when playing rock to their enemies scissors... the tactician could be in a similar pickle when facing a force led by an experienced martially inclined Outcaste,.. and you get similarly difficult problems to handle for pure ass-kickers, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T22:02:23-08:00","id":356268,"title":"","content":"I'd say after the Exaltation scene, let 'em start off with two Excellencies, and two Charms.<br /> <br /> That said, note that raising Essence to 3 explicitly doesn't take <i>any</i> training time, so while you might hold off on it for balance purposes, it's not something they have to justify with downtime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T22:18:24-08:00","id":356273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/334844-how-do-you-exalt-a-solar-circle?p=356268#post356268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say after the Exaltation scene, let 'em start off with two Excellencies, and two Charms.<br /> <br /> That said, note that raising Essence to 3 explicitly doesn't take <i>any</i> training time, so while you might hold off on it for balance purposes, it's not something they have to justify with downtime.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm looking forward to having a real selection of Essence 1 charms in EX3, from my understanding they are the sort of charms that make sense spontaneously appearing in newly exalted characters who don't really have a understanding of what they are, not like the more complex charms later down the line that manifest as something supernaturally solarish with bright halos and focused manifestation of essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T18:20:16-08:00","id":357107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/334844-how-do-you-exalt-a-solar-circle?p=356241#post356241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume the idea of not giving them all the charms and so on straight away, is so that the group isn't too imbalanced?</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly thus. The idea is to give the player a scene to be a BAMF, taking no nonsense from anybody before they scale back and spend some time &quot;Getting to know their own strengths&quot; again. That way, they are still potent, and probably shift roles somewhat, but don't occlude the NEXT BAMF Exaltation going down in the next fight over. Unless of course they surprise me and all earn their halos in one session.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/334844-how-do-you-exalt-a-solar-circle?p=356268#post356268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say after the Exaltation scene, let 'em start off with two Excellencies, and two Charms.<br /> <br /> That said, note that raising Essence to 3 explicitly doesn't take <i>any</i> training time, so while you might hold off on it for balance purposes, it's not something they have to justify with downtime.</div> </div> </div> </div>That feels about right for balance. Two Excellencies, *probably* from different Abilties (depending on the player, of course), and two Charms, giving them access to cool stuff, without being able to get high enough on the tree to get the Really crazy stuff. I like it. Thanks!<br /> <br /> The final &quot;downtime&quot; is going to be about an in-game week's time, tops, and includes every single Charm, Attribute, Ability, and Background boost they want to write down in the conversion from *Mortal to Exalted of Sol/Luna. Essence 3 is &quot;Instant&quot; but how many Mortals could really tell the difference between Ess 2 and Ess 3 the instant they Exalt? Ahem, /me sings: Getting to know me, getting to know all about me! /me ends terrible singing.<br /> <br /> However, I'm NOT going to make the suggestion of the most broken spending of Bonus Points possible, Essence 4. If somebody spots that, fine, but I ain't gonna suggest it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4623-onigato","name":"Onigato","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T23:12:21-08:00","id":357272,"title":"","content":"Something occurred to me with the idea of them exalting in rapid succession. Assuming it is a bound circle of exalted. There is every possibility while you are having your epic fight and exalting to turn the tables. That at that same moment somewhere else in Creation there is a group of solars fairing far worse in a fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}